  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022 Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) for the Venezuelan Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As Colombia moves towards regularization of thousands of Venezuelan nationals residing in Colombia, influxes continue to be of high importance with a rate of approximately 3,000 migrants and refugees entering per month according to Migraci&#xf3;n Colombia. Since October the official crossing point between Colombia and Venezuela has been reopened. Thousands of vulnerable Venezuelan migrants and refugees continue demanding humanitarian assistance and access to basic services in Colombia, whether they are in transit or planning to stay for family reunification, job opportunities or any other reason. The most sought-after services vary according to the purpose of migration, documentation, shelter, transportation, regularization, education, health services, etc. This action aims at providing safe and secure and dignified essential humanitarian aid and access to basic services for Venezuelan migrants and refugees. It also aims to prevent and mitigate protection risks by increasing opportunities to enhance resiliency amongst the migrant population and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
